        "r": 516.7599000000002,
        "b": 727.444
      },
      "content": "Air pressure forces the oil from air receiver/oil separator (AR) through oil filter (OF) and oil stop valve (Vs)to compressor element (E)."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0148",
      "reading_order": 194,
      "section": "Description",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 62.23,
        "t": 720.481,
        "r": 525.7996999999996,
        "b": 695.1039999999999
      },
      "content": "Bypass valve (BV) starts opening the supply from cooler (Co) when the oil temperature has increased to the set point. At approx. 15 °C above the set point, all the oil flows through the oil cooler."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_0149",
      "reading_order": 195,
      "section": "Description",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 62.23,
        "t": 688.141,
        "r": 500.32919999999893,
        "b": 662.7639999999999
      },
      "content": "Oil stop valve (Vs) prevents the compressor element from flooding with oil when the compressor is stopped.The valve is opened by element outlet pressure when the compressor is started."
    },
